Description: The package encompasses a range of functions for identifying
    the closest gene, exon, miRNA, or custom features—such as highly
    conserved elements and user-supplied transcription factor binding
    sites.  Additionally, users can retrieve sequences around the peaks
    and obtain enriched Gene Ontology (GO) or Pathway terms. In version
    2.0.5 and beyond, new functionalities have been introduced. These
    include features for identifying peaks associated with bi-directional
    promoters along with summary statistics (peaksNearBDP), summarizing
    motif occurrences in peaks (summarizePatternInPeaks), and associating
    additional identifiers with annotated peaks or enrichedGO
    (addGeneIDs). The package integrates with various other packages such
    as biomaRt, IRanges, Biostrings, BSgenome, GO.db, multtest, and stat
    to enhance its analytical capabilities.
